<title>SWITZERLAND: BADMINTON-SWISS OPEN RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BADMINTON-SWISS OPEN RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second round results on Wednesday in the men's singles at the Swiss Open badminton championships (prefix denotes seeding)</p>
<p>1-Poul-Erik Hoyer-Larsen (Denmark) beat Thomas Wapp (Switzerland) 15-2 15-2</p>
<p>9/16-Gang Chen (China) beat Pang Chen (Malaysia) 15-8 15-2</p>
<p>Park Sung-woo (South Korea) beat Henrik Sorensen (Denmark) 15-5 15-2</p>
<p>9/16-Hermawan Susanto (Indonesia) beat Gopi Chan (Indonesia) 15-13 15-4</p>
<p>3/4-Sun Jun (China) beat Chuen Tam Kai (Hong Kong) 15-10 15-7</p>
<p>9/16-Heryanto Arbi ((Indonesia) beat Hansen Lundgaard (Denmark) 4-15 15-11 15-7</p>
<p>Indra Wijaya (Indonesia) beat Jang Chun-woong (South Korea) 15-12 17-14</p>
<p>Henrik Bengtsson (Sweden) beat Pavel Uvarov (Russia) 15-3 15-3</p>
<p>9/16-Ardy Wiranata (Indonesia) beat Jesper Olsson (Sweden) 15-12 18-17</p>
<p>5/8-Peter Gade (Denmark) beat Deepanakar Bhattacharya (Indonesia) 15-4 2-1 (retired)</p>
<p>9/16-Dong Jiong (China) beat Peter Knowles (England) 15-10 15-3</p>
<p>Yang Zhuo (China) beat Boris Kessov (Bulgaria) 15-10 15-4</p>
<p>Xie Yangchun (China) beat 9/16-Sun Ho-hwang (South Korea) 15-7 15-11</p>
<p>5/8-Allan Budi Kusuma (Indonesia) beat Michail Popov (Bulgaria) 15-2 15-2</p>
<p>Peter Rasmussen (Denmark) beat 9/16-Luo Yigang (China) 15-7 15-7</p>
<p>2-Rashid Sidek (Malaysia) beat Oliver Pongratz (Germany) 15-1- 11-15 15-1</p>
</text>
